    <edge source="paper-0001" target="paper-0001::claim-01" id="e000001">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">MBSE creates a system model that helps integrate other discipline specific engineering models and simulations. The system level model is initiated at the start of a project and evolves throughout development. It provides a cohesive and consistent source of system requirements, design, analysis, and verification.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="paper-0001::claim-02" id="e000012">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">ModelCenter was used to integrate the analytical and simulation models. The integrated analyses were linked to the SysML model using MBSE Analyzer, a bridge between SysML tools and ModelCenter. Behavioral models were executed for a representative RAX mission to study energy state and data collection capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="paper-0001::claim-03" id="e000022">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">The time history plots show that the integrated RAX model correctly models the behavior of energy collection and data download, and their interactions.</data>
      <data key="d9">medium</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="paper-0001::claim-04" id="e000030">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">In the current practice of satellite design, tools such as STK and MATLAB are used to analyze mission performance. However, there is no readily available capability that enables verifying the impact of design decisions on mission requirements throughout the entire mission. The integrated model demonstrates how to accomplish this by performing mission simulations using MBSE models.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="paper-0001::claim-05" id="e000042">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">When the solar panel area was reduced further, to a quarter of the nominal, the energy level went below the required minimum at the end of the simulation... The results clearly show that the quarter size solar panel is too small for the mission.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="paper-0001::claim-06" id="e000052">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">When the battery capacity was reduced, energy level could not rise above the max capacity of 100,000 J. This shows that there will be spillover of energy collected by solar panel, and it may be considered to reduce the size of the solar panel.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="paper-0001::claim-07" id="e000060">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">The nominal configuration using Ann Arbor and Menlo Park stations collected about 3.9 MB of data during 24 hours... Nonetheless, all three configurations satisfy the system requirement that 'the system shall download at least 1MB of data per day'.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="paper-0001::claim-08" id="e000071">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">The RAX CubeSat model will be made available to the academic community for further study and potential extension for more complex missions.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0001" target="paper-0001::claim-09" id="e000079">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">This work was undertaken to demonstrate the power, scalability, and utility of MBSE tools and methods that are available to help meet the challenge of designing spacecraft missions of ever-increasing complexity.</data>
      <data key="d9">medium</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0002" target="paper-0002::claim-01" id="e000088">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">Abstract: 'Some of the benefits of using an MBSE approach over a traditional document-based approach are: enhanced communications, reduced development risk, improved quality, and enhanced knowledge transfer [1].' Section 2: 'the model serves as a single-source-of-truth for the development team'.</data>
      <data key="d9">medium</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0002" target="paper-0002::claim-02" id="e000097">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">Abstract: 'This approach provides a repeatable, generalized method for CubeSat development teams to follow...' Introduction: the approach 'draws from existing methodologies to provide a repeatable, generalized method for university teams'.</data>
      <data key="d9">medium</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0002" target="paper-0002::claim-03" id="e000105">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">Conclusion: 'Traceability: There is clear traceability from the mission requirements to the functionality required to satisfy those requirements.' Step 7: 'This approach uses the refine relationship... for relating the activities to use cases.'</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0002" target="paper-0002::claim-04" id="e000112">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">Step 8: 'The decomposition of activities into actions can continue down to the subsystem-level of the CubeSat. The end result can be shown in an activity hierarchy representing the full functional decomposition and the resulting functional architecture.' Conclusion: 'Recursive: The approach can be recursively applied at all levels of the mission hierarchy...'</data>
      <data key="d9">medium</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0002" target="paper-0002::claim-05" id="e000119">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">Conclusion: 'Generalizability. This approach is not dependent on any specific tool and is general enough to be easily incorporated into many systems engineering methodologies.' Introduction: 'This approach does not attempt to develop an entirely new methodology. Instead, it draws from existing methodologies...'</data>
      <data key="d9">medium</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="paper-0003::claim-01" id="e000124">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">The integrated modeling environment enables users to extract feasibility, performance, and robustness metrics. This enables visualization of both the physical states ... and functional states ... of the satellite for representative mission scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d9">medium</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="paper-0003::claim-02" id="e000135">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">Unlike these approaches, our simulation environment supports the automated flow of information between simulators, enabling users to easily evaluate different design configurations or reconfigure the analysis for different mission scenarios in a rapid and convenient way.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="paper-0003::claim-03" id="e000144">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">ParaMagic can be used to execute a given parametric model for different causalities, such that input and output variables can be switched on-the-fly.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="paper-0003::claim-04" id="e000154">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">This simulation environment enables us to evaluate design configurations, perform trade studies, and check requirements compliance. Analysis can also be automatically re-run with updated the parameter values.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="paper-0003::claim-05" id="e000167">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">vehicle and network parameters and schedules can be verified prior to being implemented, during mission operations, and can also be updated in near real-time with operational performance feedback.</data>
      <data key="d9">medium</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="paper-0003::claim-06" id="e000178">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">Using CST for this analysis allows for the interfaces to the different systems of the RAX Mission System to be analyzed and the actual information exchange between systems to be depicted and tested.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="paper-0003::claim-07" id="e000189">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">Block representation, parameterization, and state definition all serve as the glue that ties the system together, and provides the framework for integrating the design model with the analytical models.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="paper-0003::claim-08" id="e000200">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">We developed the MBSE simulation environment presented in this paper using a modular approach, which enabled easy growth of the model and multiple modelers to simultaneously contribute to the model.</data>
      <data key="d9">medium</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="paper-0003::claim-09" id="e000210">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
      <data key="d7">claimed_outcomes_value_mechanisms_evidence[]</data>
      <data key="d8">An example CubeSat model that existing and future teams can use as a template for describing and modeling their own satellites, optimizing satellite design, and evaluating mission operations.</data>
      <data key="d9">medium</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0003" target="paper-0003::claim-10" id="e000221">
      <data key="d6">HAS_CLAIM</data>
