    <edge source="paper-0023::claim-02" target="outcomecategory::effort_reduction" id="e001036">
      <data key="d6">CLAIMS_OUTCOME</data>
      <data key="d10">effort reduction</data>
      <data key="d8">Section 3.1: "The project management procedures proposed by standards like ECSS are sometimes too over-specified for nanosatellite projects which are usually undertaken by universities or academic institutions." Section 3.2: academic nanosatellite specificities allow simplifying the structure: requirements are derived from mission objectives; budget is allocated to hardware/software; "schedule and Coast Breakdown Structure can be directly derived from the Product Tree"; "students-driven projects" have changing personnel and "Business Agreement Structure can be neglected." Section 3.4: outputs for the Formal Design Phase include "Product breakdown structure (PBS)", "Work breakdown structure (WBS)", and "Cost breakdown structure (CBS)"; CBS costs are primarily hardware/software development and testing for student-driven projects.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0023::claim-02" target="outcomecategory::governance_roi" id="e001037">
      <data key="d6">CLAIMS_OUTCOME</data>
      <data key="d10">governance/ROI</data>
      <data key="d8">Section 3.1: "The project management procedures proposed by standards like ECSS are sometimes too over-specified for nanosatellite projects which are usually undertaken by universities or academic institutions." Section 3.2: academic nanosatellite specificities allow simplifying the structure: requirements are derived from mission objectives; budget is allocated to hardware/software; "schedule and Coast Breakdown Structure can be directly derived from the Product Tree"; "students-driven projects" have changing personnel and "Business Agreement Structure can be neglected." Section 3.4: outputs for the Formal Design Phase include "Product breakdown structure (PBS)", "Work breakdown structure (WBS)", and "Cost breakdown structure (CBS)"; CBS costs are primarily hardware/software development and testing for student-driven projects.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="paper-0023::claim-02" target="outcomecategory::decision_support" id="e001038">
      <data key="d6">CLAIMS_OUTCOME</data>
      <data key="d10">decision support</data>
      <data key="d8">Section 3.1: "The project management procedures proposed by standards like ECSS are sometimes too over-specified for nanosatellite projects which are usually undertaken by universities or academic institutions." Section 3.2: academic nanosatellite specificities allow simplifying the structure: requirements are derived from mission objectives; budget is allocated to hardware/software; "schedule and Coast Breakdown Structure can be directly derived from the Product Tree"; "students-driven projects" have changing personnel and "Business Agreement Structure can be neglected." Section 3.4: outputs for the Formal Design Phase include "Product breakdown structure (PBS)", "Work breakdown structure (WBS)", and "Cost breakdown structure (CBS)"; CBS costs are primarily hardware/software development and testing for student-driven projects.</data>
      <data key="d9">high</data>
    </edge>
