      <data key="d8">Section 5.1/Fig. 15: "The "Satisfied By" column shows the model elements that fulfill the requirement. For example, the "Power System" subsystem must satisfy operational requirement 100.1.6."; "The 'Verified By' column shows the specific test cases that determine how the system meets the requirement ... "Bus System Activation" activity diagram ... is used to verify operational requirement 100.1.6." Section 5.3: "The LEOP flow activity diagram is also a way to "verify" functional or operational requirements, such as the Bus System Activation state machine (Fig. 23), which verifies operational requirements 100.1.6." Fig. 23 description: Bus System Activation state machine uses LEOP Safe Mode (do/obc power on), LEOP Critical Mode, and Vbat &gt; Vsafe / Vbat &lt; Vcritic transitions to continue or recover the LEOP flow.</data>
      <data key="d9">medium</data>
